At night, I have dinner.
Now I am resting.
I sit on the sofa.
I open my laptop.
I chat with my family in Mexico.
Mother, father, and my younger sister Sofia are on the computer.
They ask, "Maya, how are you?"
I say, "I am fine."
Sofia asks, "What is your daily routine in Mumbai city?"
I say, "I wake up early in the morning."
"Then I go to the office by bus."
"Now I do my new work there."
Father asks, "How is the food there?"
I say, "The food here is delicious."
Now it is ten o'clock at night here, so I am tired.
I say, "Now I am going to sleep, goodnight."
They also say, "Goodnight Maya."
I close the laptop.
I go to bed.
I sleep peacefully.
